<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh no, bud.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> says, witnessing your accident to add another level of humiliation to your already embarrassing situation.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Did you have a little accident? It’s okay.”</span> He walks over, inspects the damage and sighs. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You really can’t be holding it in like this, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$DadNickname</span>. Go to the bathroom and take those wet clothes off and try to clean yourself up. I’ll take care of this and get you some clothes.”</span> He gives you a reassuring smile that, while nice, makes you feel like a toddler who just wet himself. <br>
<br>
You make a quick yet still embarrassing waddle to your bathroom and peel off your wet, smelly clothes. You then hop into the shower and try to wash yourself as best as you can, not wanting to walk around smelling like urine. You jump a little when the bathroom door opens and cover yourself but relax a little when you just see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> there. <br>

